    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a and b are direct: list the multiples of 6 in a range, then count them. The hardest essential demand is part c. It is heavily scaffolded, because the first and last multiples are given as 6×2 and 6×6 and the student only has to turn them into a count. The one real decision is to see that the count is the difference of the multipliers plus one (6−2+1), not 6−2. That is a small fence-post step with a link back to the list, and the student does not have to find the structure alone. This is more than a single-step divisibility check like p85-q51, but less than the linked multi-step reasoning in A3.",
